&gt;Inline rendering with document.currentScript&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Interactive Examples for Learning Shadow DOM</title><link>https://shoubhikbanerjee.github.io/blog/p/interactive-examples-for-learning-shadow-dom/</link><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 22:03:57 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://shoubhikbanerjee.github.io/blog/p/interactive-examples-for-learning-shadow-dom/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="interactive-examples-for-learning-shadow-dom"&gt;Interactive Examples for Learning Shadow DOM
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;New interactive examples are available to help users learn about shadow DOM and how shadow roots function.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="-how-it-works"&gt;🧩 How it works
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Shadow roots create isolated DOM trees that feature:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private stylesheets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Elements that interact with the page DOM in specific, controlled ways&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id="-key-details"&gt;⚙️ Key details
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The interactive examples demonstrate the following concepts:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Style encapsulation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inheritance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Slots&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JavaScript access&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#WebDevelopment #ShadowDOM #Frontend&lt;/p&gt;
